    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/trrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=039358": {
      "title": "Executive Officer Payroll",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/10/2026 Job Title : Executive Officer Payroll Pay Scale : Executive Officer Merged Closing Date : 28-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : Recruit@tcd.ie Trinity is Ireland’s leading university and is ranked 75th in the world (QS World University Rankings 2026). Founded in 1592, the University is steeped in history with a reputation for excellence in education, research, and innovation, which has been inspiring generations of thinkers for over 400 years. Thrive: Trinity College Dublin's Strategic Plan 2025 - 2030 Post ID: 039358 Post Summary: The HR Payroll Executive Officer (2 Positions) will be a key member of the university’s HR team, responsible for supporting the accurate and timely processing of the university’s payroll. The role ensures compliance with employment legislation, Revenue regulations, and internal policies, while providing a high-quality service to university staff. Payroll Services is part of the HR department and is responsible for providing HR and Payroll administrative services to the University Community of over 7,000 staff and visitors. This role works as part of a larger team of HR team that cover all HR-related administrative processes. The role reports to the Payroll Services Manager and will. Post status: Specific Purpose Contract 1 contract is for the specific purpose of filling an Executive Officer vacancy on a temporary basis pending the return of the postholder from a period of authorised leave. 1 contract is to provide back fill and support to the payroll services team for the duration of the Casual Pay Project. Hours of Post: 35 hours per week Salary: This appointment will be made on the Executive Officer Merged salary scale (€34,023- €52,232 per annum) at a point in line with current Government pay policy. monthly/weekly payscales. Closing Date: 28th October 2026 How to apply: In order to assist the selection process, applicants should submit a Curriculum Vitae and a Cover Letter (1x A4 page) that s